    {
      "title": "Making your own words",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Turkish builds new words by attaching word-forming suffixes, not by borrowing. The four suffixes below are the most common, and you can use all of them right away on words you already have."
        },
        {
          "type": "sub",
          "text": "-lı / -li / -lu / -lü — with, having"
        },
        {
          "type": "tabel",
          "head": [
            "Base word",
            "+ -lı",
            "Meaning"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "şeker (sugar)",
              "şekerli",
              "sweet, with sugar"
            ],
            [
              "süt (milk)",
              "sütlü",
              "with milk"
            ],
            [
              "et (meat)",
              "etli",
              "with meat"
            ],
            [
              "su (water)",
              "sulu",
              "juicy, with broth"
            ],
            [
              "eşya (furniture)",
              "eşyalı",
              "furnished"
            ],
            [
              "İstanbul",
              "İstanbullu",
              "a person from Istanbul"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sub",
          "text": "-sız / -siz / -suz / -süz — without"
        },
        {
          "type": "tabel",
          "head": [
            "Base word",
            "+ -sız",
            "Meaning"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "şeker",
              "şekersiz",
              "sugar-free"
            ],
            [
              "et",
              "etsiz",
              "meatless"
            ],
            [
              "tuz (salt)",
              "tuzsuz",
              "unsalted"
            ],
            [
              "su",
              "susuz",
              "waterless, thirsty"
            ],
            [
              "iş (work)",
              "işsiz",
              "unemployed"
            ],
            [
              "ev",
              "evsiz",
              "homeless"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sub",
          "text": "-cı / -ci / -cu / -cü — a person who deals with"
        },
        {
          "type": "tabel",
          "head": [
            "Base word",
            "+ -cı",
            "Meaning"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "ekmek (bread)",
              "ekmekçi",
              "baker"
            ],
            [
              "kitap",
              "kitapçı",
              "bookseller"
            ],
            [
              "balık (fish)",
              "balıkçı",
              "fisherman, fishmonger"
            ],
            [
              "çay",
              "çaycı",
              "tea seller"
            ],
            [
              "yol (road)",
              "yolcu",
              "passenger"
            ],
            [
              "emlak (property)",
              "emlakçı",
              "real-estate agent"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "After a hard letter, *c* hardens to *ç*: *kitap-çı*, *simit-çi*, *sanat-çı*. The Fıstıkçı Şahap rule again — and the memory phrase is itself an example: *fıstık* + *-çı*."
        },
        {
          "type": "sub",
          "text": "-lık / -lik / -luk / -lük — -ness, place, tool"
        },
        {
          "type": "tabel",
          "head": [
            "Base word",
            "+ -lık",
            "Meaning"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "güzel (beautiful)",
              "güzellik",
              "beauty"
            ],
            [
              "iyi (good)",
              "iyilik",
              "goodness, a favor"
            ],
            [
              "göz (eye)",
              "gözlük",
              "glasses"
            ],
            [
              "tuz (salt)",
              "tuzluk",
              "salt shaker"
            ],
            [
              "kira (rent)",
              "kiralık",
              "for rent"
            ],
            [
              "gün (day)",
              "günlük",
              "daily, diary"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "kotak",
          "title": "Four suffixes, hundreds of words",
          "items": [
            "Try it now: from *şeker*, *su*, *ev* and *çay* you can make *şekerli*, *şekersiz*, *şekerlik*, *şekerci*, *sulu*, *susuz*, *evli*, *evsiz*, *çaylı*, *çaysız*, *çaycı*, *çaylık*.",
            "Not every word you can build is actually used — but nearly all of them will be understood. This is the skill that grows your vocabulary far faster than memorizing lists."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
